From: be7000-openwrt <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: qcom-ipq9574: reset the PHY package again after the early UNIPHY bring-up

The vendor SSDK (commit 3c58ee12, "initialize manhattan after enabling
miami uniphy") GPIO-resets the QCA8084 and reruns its preinit after the
SoC UNIPHY is configured and transmitting. With the early 10G-QXGMII
bring-up the SoC now transmits before the package is configured, but
the package had already been reset at the clock controller probe, ten
seconds earlier, with no signal on the lane. Pulse the shared reset
line again right after the UNIPHY is up, when the DT hands the PCS the
line as qcom,phy-package-reset-gpios.

diff --git a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
index 54cfdfe..bead979 100644
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <linux/clk-provider.h>
 #include <linux/debugfs.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/mm.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
@@ -1652,8 +1653,30 @@ static int ipq9574_pcs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * finds the interface already set and only does the per-channel part.
 	 */
 	if (of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "qcom,early-10g-qxgmii")) {
+		struct gpio_desc *rst;
+
 		ret = ipq_pcs_config_usxgmii(qpcs, 0, PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10G_QXGMII);
 		dev_info(dev, "early 10G-QXGMII bring-up before the PHY package: %d\n", ret);
+
+		/* Second half of the vendor order (SSDK 3c58ee12): reset the PHY
+		 * package again now that the SoC side transmits, so its SerDes
+		 * comes out of reset and calibrates with a signal present. The
+		 * line is shared with the package clock controller, which pulsed
+		 * it at its own probe; nothing has been configured in the package
+		 * yet at this point, so the clock framework's view still matches
+		 * the hardware after the reset.
+		 */
+		rst = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "qcom,phy-package-reset",
+					      GPIOD_OUT_LOW | GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_NONEXCLUSIVE);
+		if (IS_ERR(rst)) {
+			dev_warn(dev, "PHY package reset gpio: %ld\n", PTR_ERR(rst));
+		} else if (rst) {
+			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(rst, 1);
+			msleep(100);
+			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(rst, 0);
+			msleep(100);
+			dev_info(dev, "PHY package reset again with UNIPHY0 up\n");
+		}
 	}
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, qpcs);
